  "observation": "Five resources per disc contain the same original menu code: two packed copies and three direct copies. All ten yield identical 153864-byte content, and the entire region matches the previously captured Disc 1 room-menu RAM at 0x801c5000. New cold-boot scenarios open the File UI in field 14 on Disc 1 and in field 290 on both discs. The UI displays two 15-slot card grids and Copy/Delete. Original code windows match all three final RAM captures. In each capture the code's menu-data pointer leads to bytes 53 43 11 01 at offset0x4b94 and the original BASLUS-00664 and BASLUS-01160 prefixes at offsets0x4fce and0x501c.",
  "interpretation": "This identifies an original menu/card-management source family on both discs and concrete original execution paths. The resident menu-context pointer, static dispatcher, card-device strings and in-memory header construction provide starting coordinates for save-format analysis. The second prefix's purpose and ordinary save-file schema remain unknown. A File menu observation and initialized header buffer do not establish card writes or a save/load round trip.",
  "confidence": "supported",
  "validation": {
    "preconditions": [
      "Exact original raw-track profiles and source-index projection hashes from EVID-REF-001/002/005/008",
      "Pinned Nix observation shell and recovered cold-boot adapters from EVID-REF-007",
      "Original reset defaults; isolated local core directories; no imported checkpoint or personal save",
      "Fresh ignored local output paths"
    ],
    "commands": [
      "nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' develop path:./nix#observation",
      "Write one exact case.scenario object from tests/reference-inputs/menu-observation-route.json to a fresh .local/scenarios JSON file.",
      "python3 tools/reference/scenario.py .local/scenarios/<case>.json --content 'discs/Xenogears disc <1-or-2>.chd' --output .local/scenarios/<fresh-output>",
      "Inspect the recorded frame sequence and final RAM. Resolve the original context pointer at0x800625a0 and its menu-data pointer at+0x32c; compare the stated source windows and header/prefix offsets.",
      "Read exact source variants from both hashed raw tracks using the original index coordinates. For the four packed copies use the bounded private transcription of original decoder0x80032eb4; compare all ten153864-byte results and the recorded original RAM region."
    ],
    "expected": "Exact source identities and code-window correspondence; bounded cold-boot input completion followed by independent visual inspection of original menu output. Save/load behavior remains unknown.",
    "actual": "All ten source variants matched. The full original region matched the existing Disc1 room-menu RAM. Three new scenario runs completed at frontend frames4407,4299,4298; their original File UIs, source instruction windows, field selectors and initialized header/prefix bytes were inspected and verified.",
    "result": "passed",
    "tolerance": "Exact source bytes, hashes, source coordinates and RAM values within the recorded configurations. No retail progression, card persistence, frame-rate or original/native equivalence claim.",
